From 25ddb4b80f1189d556e87fdcdf813916472e1848 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c4pp4
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 21:36:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] Round the Unity shadow of menus

GTK publishes the corner radius of a menu to Unity in the
_UNITY_GTK_BORDER_RADIUS property, and Unity draws the shadow of the
menu with these corners. GTK reads the radius from the menu window,
which has none, while the menu inside it has rounded corners, so the
shadow was square.

Give the menu window the radius of the menu.

Signed-off-by: c4pp4
---
 gtk/src/default/gtk-3.0/apps/_unity7.scss | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gtk/src/default/gtk-3.0/apps/_unity7.scss b/gtk/src/default/gtk-3.0/apps/_unity7.scss
index 8ed32aa4..07e696de 100644
--- a/gtk/src/default/gtk-3.0/apps/_unity7.scss
+++ b/gtk/src/default/gtk-3.0/apps/_unity7.scss
@@ -86,3 +86,9 @@ UnityPanelWidget,
 SheetStyleDialog.unity-force-quit {
     background-color: $bg_color;
 }
+
+// GTK publishes the border radius of the menu window to Unity, which
+// draws the shadow of the menu with these corners
+window.popup.unity-csd {
+    border-radius: $menu_radius;
+}
